# Prada L'Homme Intense — Zero Astra Z1 — nominal 30 mL EDP design

**Design ID:** PLI-ZERO-ASTRA-Z1  
**Date:** 2026-09-05  
**State:** COMPUTATIONAL DRAFT — not compounded, smelled, safety-approved or released; physical release remains HOLD  
**Immediate recipe parent:** NONE — explicit user instruction to start from zero  
**Target:** Prada L'Homme Intense-inspired architecture, not an exact commercial formula

## Current workflow — one computationally selected final formula

The user's 2026-09-05 instruction is **computational perfumery only**, followed by testing **one final complete blend**. The earlier plan for physical omission arms, A/B bottles and repeated bench preparations is superseded. All interim alternatives, omissions and sensitivity checks are internal computational work. No preliminary physical smell test is required to continue development or select the final candidate.

Evaluate the complete fragrance and its interactions, not independent ingredient scores alone. Resolve or explicitly bound source/stock/model uncertainty, justify retained roles against the target and freeze one complete formula for handoff. A model-selected final candidate is distinct from a physically validated fragrance. The user's later whole-blend test will assess the composition as a whole; it will not retroactively establish causal proof for each ingredient's contribution.

This is a workflow-only amendment: Z1's ingredients, doses, stock fractions, carrier accounting and original simulation outputs are unchanged. Z1 remains the computational working draft; this amendment does not declare it the final selected formula. The historical raw report below is preserved, including its empirical-authority warnings; those warnings are not instructions to conduct preliminary physical trials.

## The new design

A floral iris body sits above warm sandalwood, with a dry root-to-cedar seam, earthy patchouli, dry amber and a rounded but restrained tonka interior. The hypothesis is that distinct textures can remain readable without turning into a heavy wood-amber blanket. This is an intended smell, not an observed result.

Four woods are selected deliberately: **Sandalore, Ebanol, Cedarwood oil Virginia and Iso E Super**. Sandalore provides body; Ebanol a stronger sandalwood accent; cedar the grain; Iso E Super abstract woody space. These are not four interchangeable ways to increase a wood score. Sandalore/Ebanol is the closest potential overlap and is the first computational nonredundancy question. Patchouli and Ambrox add separate earthy and amber functions; Dihydro Beta Ionone is an iris-to-wood connector.

The official target includes iris, amber, patchouli, sandalwood and roasted tonka. It does not disclose a formula or require a leather accord. [Prada official description](https://www.prada.com/ww/en/p/lhomme-prada-intense-edp-100-ml/2A1252_2HC1_F0Z99_P_ML100)

This is a new lineage, not V2 with extra woods. V1/V2 doses, row count and recipe-preservation rules were not carried forward. Seventeen selected products are the present consequence of the roles, not a quality target or a permanent minimum.

## TARGET / IDEAL — frozen before stock conversion

The independent functional budget is **340 iris / 270 wood / 90 tonka / 100 amber-patchouli / 150 floral air / 50 musk = 1000 supplied-product mass parts**. These percentages are not perceived contribution. Full material allocations, strongest alternatives and primary-source provenance are in [the zero-origin ideal](../docs/research/Prada_LHomme_Intense_Zero_Astra_Z1_Ideal.md).

| Material | Ideal product parts | Role hypothesis |
|---|---:|---|
| Patchouli EO | 65 | The named patchouli anchor, contrasting dry wood with earthy depth. |
| Ambrox Super | 35 | Dry amber thread beside patchouli and tonka; not a claim to reproduce all commercial amber chemistry. |
| Hedione | 105 | Floral spacing around iris, evaluated against an omission rather than assumed radiance. |
| Hexyl Salicylate | 35 | Quiet floral/dry-bark blending support between Hedione, iris and cedar; no guaranteed projection claim. |
| Linalyl Acetate | 10 | A small aromatic-floral approach to the iris, not a citrus/fougere lead. |
| Alpha-Isomethyl Ionone | 285 | Powdered floral iris body; the dominant thematic scaffold. |
| Dihydro Beta Ionone | 40 | Woody iris passage between floral body and cedar grain. |
| Alpha Irone | 10 | Specific irone accent and creamy orris identity. |
| Orivone | 5 | Small earthy-root edge against creamy iris and sandalwood. |
| Romandolide | 50 | One soft balsamic musk layer connecting the iris and warm base. |
| Tonkarome | 45 | Rounded tonka interior; roasted character is a sensory target, not certified product chemistry. |
| Coumarin | 40 | Dry hay-tonka definition against the round Tonkarome body. |
| Heliotropal | 5 | Small almond-powder junction linking iris to the tonka section. |
| Iso E Super | 110 | Abstract woody space around the explicit sandalwood and cedar. |
| Sandalore | 110 | Continuous warm sandalwood body. |
| Cedarwood oil Virginia | 35 | Dry recognizable wood grain connecting iris root to the base. |
| Ebanol | 15 | Focused sandalwood accent above the body. |
| **Total** | **1000** | |

Sandalore versus Bacdanol was a body choice; Ebanol versus Javanol an accent choice; Virginia cedar versus Vertofix a grain/bridge choice. The rejected whole architecture was Bacdanol + Vertofix + Kephalis + Clearwood: plausible, but more of the warm/dark character would reside in the woods themselves and compete with the independent tonka/amber section. Cashmeran would add textile warmth, not the same wood-grain function. Azarbre and Amberwood F do not yet earn distinct roles.

Within iris, AIMI is the broad floral body, Alpha Irone the specific irone accent, Dihydro Beta Ionone the woody passage, and Orivone the small root edge. No Orris Liquid is treated as an assayed natural or as a duplicate irone stock. Tonkarome and Coumarin are a deliberately challenged body/definition pair, with a small Heliotropal almond-powder junction. Whether this reads as roasted tonka rather than generic sweet powder is an explicit unresolved acceptance question.

One Romandolide layer is selected for the soft balsamic-musk connection. Habanolide's metallic-clean and Ambrettolide's ambrette-fruity directions were considered but not automatically stacked. No depleted Tonalide, Macrolide, Musk Ketone or Polysantol is used.

